    "created_at": "2016-10-12T14:59:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-12T14:59:06Z",
    "body": "@annevk thanks for pinging me on this.\n\nMy sense is that the CSSWG does not currently have a strong position about what should be in the UA stylesheet about applying `user-select:none` to a few things, but as the css-ui-4 spec stabilizes, we may eventually get to that point.\n\nBased on this, I think the proposed wording is OK but not ideal: saying that it is up to the UA seems to imply that there intentionally will be no normative requirement either way. I think it would be better to state that this is \"undefined in this specification\" or something along these lines.\n\nAs for @sideshowbarker 's comment, no strong feeling from me either way.\n\nAs a side note, this reminds me that I've been wanting for some terminology anchors that relate to this discussion. Do we have a word for \"elements that are normally writable/editable, but currently aren't because they're either in readonly or disabled state\", or for \"elements that are normally writable/editable, regardless of whether they currently aren't because of being either in readonly or disabled state\"? If we don't, could we make something up? See https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/285 for an instance of wanting this. (Also, let me know if I should raise that as a separate issue).\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/253238322/reactions",
