    "created_at": "2016-10-12T15:34:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-12T15:34:29Z",
    "body": "> I think it would be better to state that this is \"undefined in this specification\" or something along these lines.\n\nThat makes sense to me; will change.\n\n> Do we have a word for \"elements that are normally writable/editable, but currently aren't because they're either in readonly or disabled state\"\n\nI think \"not mutable\" might be what you're looking for?\n\n>  \"elements that are normally writable/editable, regardless of whether they currently aren't because of being either in readonly or disabled state\"\n\n\"form controls\"?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
