    "created_at": "2016-10-12T15:50:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-12T15:50:45Z",
    "body": "> > Do we have a word for \"elements that are normally writable/editable, but currently aren't because they're either in readonly or disabled state\"\n> \n> I think \"not mutable\" might be what you're looking for?\n> \n> >   \"elements that are normally writable/editable, regardless of whether they currently aren't because of being either in readonly or disabled state\"\n> \n> \"form controls\"?\n> It's not all form controls, since buttons are excluded. And not just form controls, since Editing Hosts (contentEditable=true) are included.\n\nThe terminology I'm considering establishing for the sake of CSS specs if I can't find anything better is this:\n\n> an editable element is either an editing host or a form control with normally mutable textual content such as textarea, even if this form control is in non mutable state.\n\nIt looks like it should work, but the phrasing doesn't look great to me, and I am kind of surprised there isn't already a word for this.\n",
